      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Douglas G. Benedon)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question -- excuse me. The question presented should be answered with the following bright line rule: Imposition of vicarious liability under the FHA should be determined by application of established rules of corporate and agency law not criteria unique to the FHA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Suppose -- suppose that I were to agree with you and the Court were to agree with you as to your criticism of the Ninth Circuit's reasoning and -- and that it agreed with you too that general principles of agency and corporate liability apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we were prepared -- certainly at the summary judgment stage, Justice Scalia, we would -- we would have been happy to go forward with proof of underfunding, and there is substantial proof of underfunding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Now, as I understand the California law, this broker could not operate under that license on his own. The only way he could use that license was as an officer of the corporation. Isn't that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schwemm",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHWEMM: Ordinarily, Your Honor, but not in this case. I -- I repeat. This company cannot be a broker if it doesn't have a broker-qualified individual who takes responsibility for the agents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, do we look to general Federal common law agency principles, or are we bound by State agency law, Mr. Stewart?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "936b571c7424af0c458b34f8237eb6243c3a8d1f46c4577922880070200b99e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-936b571c7424-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district judge first threw out on 12(b)(6) everything except the claim against Mr. Meyer as designated officer/broker, and subsequently entered summary judgment for the petitioner on that claim."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
